hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1117","Ali bin Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami and Abdul-Quddus bin Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Al-Habhab told us, and this is the wording of the hadith of Abdul Al-Quddus, Amr i.e. Ibn Asim told me, Hammam told me, Qatada told me, on the authority of An-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever forgets the two rak’ahs of dawn, let him pray them when the sun rises.”"
